 **Notes:**
 - The fitted frailty variance quantifies unobserved frailty heterogeneity and selection-induced depletion within cohorts at rebased enrollment time. Near-zero values indicate weak identifiability or effectively linear cumulative hazards under the working model.
-- Each entry reports the fitted variance rounded to two decimal places; the stored results retain full precision.
-- The "All ages (full population)" row fits the supplied aggregate counts, including unknown birth years.
+- Frailty intervals use the raw constrained optimizer estimates; zeros denote values rounded to two decimals or the lower boundary. \* The dose-2 estimates at ages 50–59 and 60–69 concentrate at zero despite limited local information for small positive variances. A boundary-piled bootstrap is not a calibrated interval for the underlying variance. The 40–49 dose-2 fitted value is poorly resolved across the entire allowed range. KCOR intervals retain the existing upper-bound zero-variance fallback (287 of 999 dose-2 draws at ages 40–49). Source: `analysis/s6/all-age-precision.json` and its matched draws.
+- The "All ages" row fits the supplied full-population aggregate counts, including unknown birth years.
 - Table @tbl:si_raw_hazards reports raw outcome contrasts for ages 40–99 and the supplied full-population total.
 
